[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/401318523","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/5293#issuecomment-401318523","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/5293","id":401318523,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQwMTMxODUyMw==","user":{"login":"ilevkivskyi","id":12005495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDA1NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12005495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi","html_url":"https://github.com/ilevkivskyi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ilevkivskyi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-06-29T10:42:28Z","updated_at":"2018-06-29T10:42:28Z","body":"OK, the solution is super-simple here. Since named tuple variables are \"artificial\" (auto-generated), and therefore are always created directly as a `Var` with `is_property` set to `True`, they are not identified as immutable by protocol check (it looks for a `property` decorator).\r\n\r\nSo it would be just one line fix in `subtypes.get_member_flags`, we need to add a check for `v.is_property` in this code:\r\n```pthon\r\n    # just a variable\r\n    if isinstance(v, Var):\r\n        flags = {IS_SETTABLE}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWould you like to make a PR?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/